  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Bathymetric Contours",
  "description": "Data Type: Ocean/Coasts ; This layer contains bathymetric contours (20m interval) for the Exxon Valdez oil spill area as distributed by the Alaska Department of Natural Resources (DNR). The Alaska DNR data is based primarily on National Ocean Service (NOS) data. NOS publishes digital bathymetric data in two forms: raw depths of all soundings from included bathymetric surveys, and \"gridded\" data (a summarization of the raw data information). Gridded data is a summarization of raw NOS data information and includes the mean, maximum, and minimum depths recorded in each cell in a 15 second latitude by 15 second longitude grid. The Alaska DNR augmented the gridded data with information from NOAA nautical charts and converted it to bathymetric contours (interval = 20 m). Please see documentation for bath_pl and bath_pt for related databases.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: Unknown",
